From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:10:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: say a sleep ended before its commit,
 not that the GPU refused it

When another device refuses a deep sleep after the GPU's .prepare, the
sleep never reaches the commit that would stop the GPU firmware, and the
GPU's .complete finds the stop it left there unrun. It logged that as
"sleep refused before the commit: GPU firmware never stopped", which
reads as the GPU refusing the sleep. On the J604 it followed apple_sep's
refusal (dpm_suspend -2) and was taken for a second one.

Say what happened: the sleep ended before its commit, refused elsewhere,
and the firmware was left running. A refusal by the GPU itself is still
"GPU refused sleep" from .prepare.

Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit a87812f05d9569ab4251287b2502ef7a53c4f917)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/sleep.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/sleep.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/sleep.rs
index 94c65491df..375ff723cc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/sleep.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/sleep.rs
@@ -302,7 +302,7 @@ fn sleep_complete(&self) {
         if self.shared.sleep_commit_finish() == Some(false) && !real {
             dev_info!(
                 self.shared.dev.as_ref(),
-                "sleep refused before the commit: GPU firmware never stopped\n"
+                "sleep ended before its commit (refused elsewhere): GPU firmware left running\n"
             );
             self.shared.sleeping.store(false, Ordering::Release);
             self.shared.poll_now();
